IMPORT prelude

-- Economic Expansion Incentives (Relief from Income Tax) Act 1967 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a company that holds, or
-- wants, one of its tax incentives: the closing dates for new approvals (ss 5(4), 17(4), 21(4), 33(6), 37(4), 43(7)-(10)); the
-- length of a pioneer tax relief period (s 6) and of a development and expansion relief period (ss 22, 23); the development and
-- expansion concessionary rate and its rising floor (s 21(9)-(19), (23)); approved foreign loans and approved royalties (ss 33, 34,
-- 35(4), 36, 38, 39(5), 40); investment allowances (ss 44, 46, 47); and show-cause before revocation (s 61).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to and including 1 December 2021), informal consolidation, version in
-- force from 25/12/2024, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EEIRITA1967.txt. The latest amendment annotated in the text
-- is Act 41 of 2024 (wef 25/12/2024). The arrangement of sections at the head of the deposit is one row out of step with the body;
-- the body's numbering is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0078 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act applies only to companies (every incentive is applied for by "a company"); an individual meets it only
-- through a company. SCOPED to the decisions a company meets most often. Not encoded: the ascertainment of income, old and new trade
-- and separate-trade rules (ss 7-12, 25-28); the loss and allowance carry-forward order (s 15); intellectual property income (s 19);
-- transfer of awards (Part 5); approved activities (Part 7 Division 2, ss 40A-40G); corporate partnerships and the crediting
-- mechanics between the normal and concessionary allowance accounts (ss 42, 45); the recovery assessments (ss 14, 24, 61A); saved
-- repealed Parts (s 65); and every regulation or "such earlier date as may be prescribed" (none was retrieved).
--
-- DATES are written as numbers of the form YYYYMMDD (1 January 2029 is 20290101), so that "on or after" is AT LEAST.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Economic Expansion Incentives (Relief from Income Tax) Act 1967 -- incentives`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

DECLARE Incentive IS ONE OF
    `pioneer enterprise`
    `pioneer service company`
    `development and expansion company`
    `approved foreign loan`
    `approved royalties, fees or contributions`
    `investment allowance for manufacturing, services, R&D, construction, water, tourism or satellites`
    `investment allowance for energy efficiency`
    `investment allowance for a submarine cable system`
    `investment allowance for reducing greenhouse gas emissions`

§§ `5(4), 17(4), 21(4), 33(6), 37(4), 43(7)-(10) -- when a new approval may still be given`

-- s 5(4): "No company may be approved as a pioneer enterprise on or after 1 January 2029." s 17(4) (pioneer service company) and
-- s 21(4) (development and expansion company) say the same; s 33(6): the Minister "may not approve any loan as an approved foreign
-- loan on or after 1 January 2029". s 37(4): no approved royalties, fees or contributions "on or after 1 April 2023".
-- s 43(8): no investment allowance approval for a project under s 43(1)(a) to (h) "on or after 1 January 2029 or such earlier date as
-- may be prescribed"; (7) energy efficiency "from and including 1 April 2010 up to and including 31 December 2026"; (9) submarine
-- cable systems from 20 February 2018 to 31 December 2028; (10) reducing greenhouse gas emissions from 1 April 2021 to
-- 31 December 2026 -- each "or such earlier date as may be prescribed" (prescribed earlier dates are not modelled).
GIVEN `the incentive` IS AN Incentive, `the approval date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new approval may be given` IF
    CONSIDER `the incentive`
    WHEN `approved royalties, fees or contributions` THEN `the approval date` LESS THAN 20230401
    WHEN `investment allowance for energy efficiency` THEN `the approval date` AT LEAST 20100401 AND `the approval date` AT MOST 20261231
    WHEN `investment allowance for a submarine cable system` THEN `the approval date` AT LEAST 20180220 AND `the approval date` AT MOST 20281231
    WHEN `investment allowance for reducing greenhouse gas emissions` THEN `the approval date` AT LEAST 20210401 AND `the approval date` AT MOST 20261231
    OTHERWISE `the approval date` LESS THAN 20290101

§§ `6 -- the pioneer tax relief period`

-- s 6(1): the period "commences on the production day ... and continues for such period, not exceeding 15 years, as the Minister may
-- determine". (2): extensions "not exceeding 5 years at any one time". (3): "The total tax relief period for a pioneer product,
-- together with all extensions, must not in total exceed 15 years." s 18 applies ss 6 to 15 to pioneer service companies.
GIVEN `initial years` IS A NUMBER, `longest single extension` IS A NUMBER, `all extensions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pioneer relief period is within the Act` IF
        `initial years` AT MOST 15
    AND `longest single extension` AT MOST 5
    AND `initial years` PLUS `all extensions` AT MOST 15

§§ `22, 23 -- the development and expansion tax relief period`

-- s 22(1): the period continues "(a) for such period not exceeding 10 years" and "(b) for such further period or periods, not
-- exceeding 5 years for each period"; (2) extensions "not exceeding 5 years at any one time"; (3) the total "must not in the aggregate
-- exceed 20 years". (4): for a "relevant development and expansion company" the Minister may extend "beyond the maximum total period
-- allowed under subsection (3)" by periods "not exceeding 10 years at any one time"; (5) aggregate not to exceed 40 years; (6) such an
-- extension "may only be granted during the period between 18 February 2008 and 31 December 2028 (both dates inclusive)". (7): a
-- relevant company oversees the activity "on a regional or global basis", or engages in a services activity under s 20 para (b)/(c).
-- s 23(1): international legal services approved "between 1 April 2010 and 30 June 2017 (both dates inclusive)" get "a
-- non-extendable period of 5 years" and tax "at the rate of 10%"; (2) not for a company approved under s 13S of the Income Tax Act.
GIVEN `years already granted` IS A NUMBER, `extension years` IS A NUMBER, `is a relevant company` IS A BOOLEAN, `extension date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a development and expansion extension is within the Act` IF
        (`extension years` AT MOST 5 AND `years already granted` PLUS `extension years` AT MOST 20)
    OR  (    `is a relevant company`
         AND `extension years` AT MOST 10
         AND `years already granted` PLUS `extension years` AT MOST 40
         AND `extension date` AT LEAST 20080218
         AND `extension date` AT MOST 20281231)

GIVEN `approval date` IS A NUMBER, `approved under s 13S` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the international legal services rule applies` IF
        `approval date` AT LEAST 20100401
    AND `approval date` AT MOST 20170630
    AND (NOT `approved under s 13S`)

§§ `21(10), (11), (17A) -- the initial concessionary rate`

-- s 21(10): the initial rate is "(a) in the case of a development and expansion company approved as such before 19 April 2016, a
-- concessionary rate of not less than 5%" or "(b) in any other case, 5%, 10% or 15%". (17A): "For the purposes of subsections (10)(b),
-- (11), (13) and (16), the Minister may, on or after 17 February 2024 -- (a) specify the concessionary rate of 15% in the certificate
-- ... but only for any expansion income that is derived on or after 1 January 2024."
-- (17A) names (10)(b), not (10)(a): a company approved before 19 April 2016 may have any rate of 5% or more, 15% included, at any time.
GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER, `approval date` IS A NUMBER, `date the rate is specified` IS A NUMBER, `income derived from` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the initial concessionary rate is permitted` IF
    IF `approval date` LESS THAN 20160419
    THEN `the rate` AT LEAST 5
    ELSE     `the rate` EQUALS 5
         OR  `the rate` EQUALS 10
         OR  (    `the rate` EQUALS 15
              AND `date the rate is specified` AT LEAST 20240217
              AND `income derived from` AT LEAST 20240101)

§§ `21(13), (13A), (17), (23) -- the rising floor for a specified development and expansion company`

-- s 21(17): the parts of a tax relief period are (a) the 11th to the 15th year; (b) the 16th to the 20th; (c) the 21st to the 30th;
-- (d) the 31st to the 40th. (23): a "milestone date" is "the first day of any part".
-- (13): for a "specified development and expansion company" the rate in a relevant part ("part X") "must not be less than
-- [(0.5 x B) + A]%". (13A): A is 5%, 10% or 15%; where A is 5% or 10% each of parts (a) to (d) is a relevant part, and where A is 15%
-- only parts (c) and (d); B is the number of milestone dates of those relevant parts on which the company was a specified company and
-- that have transpired up to and including the milestone date of part X.
-- (23): a specified company is one approved on or after 29 February 2012, or granted an extension on or after that date ((24): only
-- as from the first day of the extension).
-- This encoding ASSUMES the company was a specified company on every milestone date reached (so B counts every relevant part up to
-- part X); a company that became specified part-way through would have a smaller B.
GIVEN `year of the relief period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part number` MEANS
    IF `year of the relief period` AT MOST 10 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `year of the relief period` AT MOST 15 THEN 1
         ELSE IF `year of the relief period` AT MOST 20 THEN 2
              ELSE IF `year of the relief period` AT MOST 30 THEN 3
                   ELSE 4

GIVEN `base rate A` IS A NUMBER, `year of the relief period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the milestone count B` MEANS
    IF `base rate A` EQUALS 15
    THEN `the larger of` 0 (`the part number` `year of the relief period` MINUS 2)
    ELSE `the part number` `year of the relief period`

GIVEN `base rate A` IS A NUMBER, `year of the relief period` IS A NUMBER, `is a specified company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lowest concessionary rate for the year` MEANS
    IF `is a specified company`
    THEN 0.5 TIMES `the milestone count B` `base rate A` `year of the relief period` PLUS `base rate A`
    ELSE `base rate A`

GIVEN `approval date` IS A NUMBER, `extension grant date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a specified development and expansion company` IF
    `approval date` AT LEAST 20120229 OR `extension grant date` AT LEAST 20120229

§§ `21(9), (18), (19) -- expansion income and the tax on it`

-- s 21(9): tax at the concessionary rate "is levied ... upon the expansion income". (18): "The expansion income is the income from
-- such qualifying activity ... that exceeds the average corresponding income." (19): the average corresponding income is "one-third of
-- the total of the corresponding qualifying income for the 3 years immediately preceding the commencement day". (22): the Minister may
-- specify any other amount instead (not modelled).
GIVEN `qualifying income` IS A NUMBER, `prior year 1` IS A NUMBER, `prior year 2` IS A NUMBER, `prior year 3` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the expansion income` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 (`qualifying income` MINUS (`prior year 1` PLUS `prior year 2` PLUS `prior year 3`) DIVIDED BY 3)

GIVEN `qualifying income` IS A NUMBER, `prior year 1` IS A NUMBER, `prior year 2` IS A NUMBER, `prior year 3` IS A NUMBER, `rate in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concessionary tax on expansion income` MEANS
    `the expansion income` `qualifying income` `prior year 1` `prior year 2` `prior year 3` TIMES `rate in percent` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `33, 34, 36 -- approved foreign loans`

-- s 33(1): a company with a loan "of not less than $20 million from a non-resident person" for productive equipment "may apply";
-- (2) the Minister "may, where the Minister thinks it expedient to do so, consider an application" for less than $20 million.
-- s 34: equipment financed from an approved foreign loan "must not be sold, transferred, or otherwise disposed of without the prior
-- written permission of the Minister, unless the loan has been repaid in full".
-- s 36(3): a company that extends the repayment period "must give written notice thereof to the Minister within 30 days".
GIVEN `loan amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company may apply as of right` IF `loan amount` AT LEAST 20000000

GIVEN `disposed of the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN, `had the Minister's prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `loan repaid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 34 is contravened` IF
    `disposed of the equipment` AND (NOT `had the Minister's prior written permission`) AND (NOT `loan repaid in full`)

§§ `38, 35(4), 39(5), 40 -- approved royalties, fees and contributions`

-- s 38(1): if approved royalties cease to be payable early the company must give notice "within 30 days". (2): the company "must not,
-- without the prior sanction of the Minister, amend or otherwise vary the terms ... except in cases where for the same consideration the
-- amount ... is to be reduced and in that event the company must notify the Minister accordingly within 30 days".
-- s 39(5) (and s 35(4) for loans): the Minister for finance may waive the debt arising from a revocation "under subsection (2)" if
-- satisfied "the company did not knowingly or intentionally contravene". A revocation under s 61 is not mentioned.
-- s 40: where the tax on approved royalties is at a reduced rate and they "have been expended in the acquisition of ordinary share
-- capital in the company from which those payments were received, the amount of income equal to that expenditure is exempt from tax".
GIVEN `varied the terms` IS A BOOLEAN, `had the Minister's sanction` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reduction for the same consideration` IS A BOOLEAN, `days until notice of the reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 38(2) is contravened` IF
        `varied the terms`
    AND (NOT `had the Minister's sanction`)
    AND (    (NOT `a reduction for the same consideration`)
         OR  `days until notice of the reduction` GREATER THAN 30)

GIVEN `revoked under the section's own power` IS A BOOLEAN, `contravened knowingly or intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt may be waived` IF
    `revoked under the section's own power` AND (NOT `contravened knowingly or intentionally`)

GIVEN `reduced-rate royalties` IS A NUMBER, `spent on ordinary shares of the payer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the royalty income exempt under section 40` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `reduced-rate royalties` `spent on ordinary shares of the payer`

§§ `44 -- the investment allowance`

-- s 44(1): the allowance is "a specified percentage, not exceeding 100% of the amount (which may be subject to a specified maximum) of
-- the fixed capital expenditure" incurred within the qualifying period, which runs from the investment day and is "(i) not exceeding
-- 5 years; or (ii) not exceeding 8 years where the specified item is acquired under a hire-purchase agreement made on or after
-- 15 February 2007"; and (b) for a tourism project under s 43(1)(g) "not exceeding 10 years".
GIVEN `percentage` IS A NUMBER, `fixed capital expenditure` IS A NUMBER, `specified maximum expenditure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investment allowance` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `percentage` 100 TIMES `the smaller of` `fixed capital expenditure` `specified maximum expenditure` DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `a tourism project` IS A BOOLEAN, `hire-purchase agreement date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest qualifying period in years` MEANS
    IF `a tourism project` THEN 10
    ELSE IF `hire-purchase agreement date` AT LEAST 20070215 THEN 8
         ELSE 5

§§ `46 -- disposing of assets that earned an allowance`

-- s 46(1): "During its qualifying period or within 2 years after the end of its qualifying period, a company must not, without the
-- Minister's written approval, sell, lease out or otherwise dispose of any assets in respect of which an investment allowance has been
-- given." (2): the allowance "may be recovered": deducted from the account, and where the account "is insufficient", an assessment
-- for "the amount unrecovered". (3): the Minister may waive recovery (not modelled).
-- Two years after a YYYYMMDD date is that number plus 20000.
GIVEN `disposal date` IS A NUMBER, `end of the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER, `had the Minister's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the allowance may be recovered` IF
        `disposal date` AT MOST `end of the qualifying period` PLUS 20000
    AND (NOT `had the Minister's written approval`)

GIVEN `allowance on the asset` IS A NUMBER, `account balance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount to be assessed` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 (`allowance on the asset` MINUS `account balance`)

§§ `47 -- using the allowance account`

-- s 47(1): where the normal investment allowance account is in credit, "(a) an amount of the chargeable normal income, not exceeding
-- the credit ... is exempt from tax" and "(b) any remaining balance ... is to be carried forward" to the next year with chargeable
-- normal income. (4) is the same for the concessionary account. (3): an election to use the normal account against concessionary
-- income must be made "at the time of lodgment of the return of income".
GIVEN `chargeable income` IS A NUMBER, `account credit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income exempt under section 47` MEANS `the smaller of` `chargeable income` `account credit`

GIVEN `chargeable income` IS A NUMBER, `account credit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit carried forward` MEANS
    `account credit` MINUS `the income exempt under section 47` `chargeable income` `account credit`

§§ `60, 61 -- confidentiality and revocation`

-- s 60(1): the contents of any application, certificate or letter "must not, except at the instance of the company, be published";
-- (2) the Minister may gazette the company's name and "the industry and product or produce to which the certificate or letter relates".
-- s 61(1): on a contravention the Minister "may, by written notice, require the company within 30 days from the date of service of
-- the notice to show cause"; (2) may then revoke "with effect from a date determined by the Minister"; s 61A(1): that date "may be a
-- date that is before the date on which notice ... is given (including a date before the date of contravention)".
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `the company's name`
    `the industry and product`
    `the contents of the application`
    `the terms of the certificate`

GIVEN `what` IS A Disclosure, `at the company's instance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it may be published` IF
        `at the company's instance`
    OR  CONSIDER `what`
        WHEN `the company's name` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the industry and product` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `days since service of the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is still within time to show cause` IF `days since service of the notice` AT MOST 30
